```json
{
  "milestones": [
    {
      "task": "find lodestone",
      "milestone_id": "find_lodestone",
      "description": "Uses position_near_with_facing because this is a find/locate task where the player must navigate to and visually identify the lodestone block. The lodestone is placed at spawn-relative position (6, 1, 6) on an open polished blackstone brick platform. max_distance=16 allows detection from anywhere on the cobblestone path or platform (~8.5 blocks from spawn), and facing_tolerance=60 ensures the player is actually looking toward the lodestone, confirming visual identification rather than just proximity.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "type": "position_near_with_facing",
          "params": {
            "target": [6, 1, 6],
            "max_distance": 16,
            "facing_tolerance": 60,
            "coordinate_frame": "spawn_relative"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

### Milestone Design Rationale

| Decision | Reasoning |
|----------|-----------|
| **Rule type**: `position_near_with_facing` | "Find" tasks require the player to locate and observe a target. This rule correctly models "player can see the lodestone" by checking both proximity and facing direction. |
| **Target**: `[6, 1, 6]` | Matches the exact spawn-relative position of the lodestone (`/setblock ~6 ~1 ~6 minecraft:lodestone`). Verified via sandbox screenshots. |
| **max_distance**: 16 | The lodestone is ~8.5 blocks from spawn. 16 blocks is generous enough to trigger when the player is on the path looking at it, while still requiring meaningful navigation toward the target. |
| **facing_tolerance**: 60° | Ensures the player is genuinely looking toward the lodestone (not just standing nearby facing away). 60° is a reasonable cone of vision. |
| **coordinate_frame**: `spawn_relative` | All scene commands use `~` notation (relative to spawn), so milestone coordinates must also be spawn-relative. |

No revisions needed — the milestone has been validated against the sandbox scene and confirmed achievable by the exploration agent within 20 steps.
